lesson: 185
title: Cuts and pieces
level: primary-3
stars: 2
explain: Cutting a log or a ribbon into pieces always takes one cut fewer than the number of pieces: the last piece needs no cut.
explain: A log of 24 dm cut into pieces of 4 dm gives 24 ÷ 4 = 6 pieces, which takes 6 - 1 = 5 cuts.
explain: If each cut takes 3 minutes, the work takes 5 × 3 = 15 minutes, not 6 × 3.
vars: a=name p=2..9 n=3..12 m=2..9
let: len = n * p
answer: (n - 1) * m
exercise: A log is {len} dm long. {a} saws it into pieces {p} dm long. Each cut takes {m} minutes. How many minutes does {a.he} need?
exercise: {a} cuts a ribbon {len} cm long into pieces of {p} cm. One cut takes {m} seconds. How many seconds does all the cutting take?
exercise: A pipe {len} m long is cut into equal parts of {p} m each. Every cut takes {m} minutes. How long does the cutting take in minutes?
exercise: {a} saws a board of {len} dm into pieces of {p} dm. It takes {m} minutes to make one cut. How many minutes does {a.he} saw?
exercise: A rope of {len} m is cut into pieces of {p} m. Each cut takes {m} seconds. How many seconds are spent cutting?
test: It takes {a} {m} minutes to saw through a beam once. How many minutes will it take {a.him} to turn a {len} dm beam into pieces each {p} dm long?
test: A worker spends {m} seconds on every cut. How many seconds does the worker spend dividing a {len} cm strip of paper into {p} cm strips?
test: A {len} m cable must be cut into sections {p} m long, and each cut takes {m} minutes. How many minutes of cutting are needed?
exercise: How many minutes does {a} need to saw a {len} dm log into {p} dm pieces, if each cut takes {m} minutes?
exercise: A carpenter in Maine cuts a plank {len} dm long into pieces of {p} dm. One cut takes {m} minutes. How long does the cutting take, in minutes?
exercise: A ribbon of {len} cm; pieces of {p} cm; {m} seconds per cut. How many seconds of cutting?
exercise: {a} in Leeds cuts a roll of paper {len} cm long into strips {p} cm long, and every cut takes {m} seconds. How many seconds does it take in total?
exercise: A steel bar of {len} dm is cut into equal pieces of {p} dm in a workshop in Ontario. Each cut takes {m} minutes. How many minutes are spent on cutting altogether?
exercise: {a} cuts a loaf of bread {len} cm long into slices {p} cm thick. Each cut takes {m} seconds. How many seconds does {a.he} spend cutting?
exercise: A tree trunk in New Zealand is {len} m long. A woodcutter saws it into logs {p} m long, taking {m} minutes per cut. How many minutes does the sawing take?
exercise: Every cut of a pipe takes a plumber in Dublin {m} minutes. The pipe is {len} m long and is cut into pieces {p} m long. How many minutes does the plumber spend cutting?
test: {a} snaps a {len} cm stick of toffee into pieces {p} cm long, and each snap takes {m} seconds. How many seconds does all the snapping take?
test: How long, in minutes, does it take to saw a {len} dm fence rail into {p} dm lengths when every saw cut lasts {m} minutes?
test: A tailor in London needs {m} seconds for one snip. How many seconds does she need to cut a {len} cm strip of cloth into pieces {p} cm long?
test: A baker in Texas divides a {len} cm roll of dough into pieces {p} cm long. One cut takes {m} seconds. How much time do the cuts take, in seconds?
test: {m} minutes for each cut: how many minutes in all to saw a {len} dm log in Canada into {n} equal pieces?
test: A gardener in Sydney cuts a {len} m hose into {p} m pieces. If one cut needs {m} seconds, how many seconds does the job take?
exercise: log's {len} dm, {a} saws it in {p} dm bits, each cut {m} mins. how long all up
exercise: ribbon {len} cm, cut into {p} cm pieces, {m} secs a cut. how many secs total
exercise: plank {len} dm, chopping into {p} dm bits, takes {m+1} — nah sorry, {m} mins per cut. how many mins
exercise: Sam says {n} pieces so {n} cuts, {n}×{m}. nah thats wrong. ribbon {len} cm into {p} cm bits, {m} secs a cut, how many secs
test: {a} chops a {len} cm baguette into {p} cm chunks, each chop {m} secs. how many secs choppin
test: pipe's {len} dm, need {p} dm bits, one cut = {m} min (saw cost 15 bucks lol). minutes in total?
test: Mia reckons {n}×{m} minutes. nah. {len} dm log into {p} dm pieces, {m} mins each cut — how many mins really
exercise: The old oak in the late Mr Green's garden was cut down. A log {len} dm long is sawn into pieces {p} dm long, and each cut takes {m} minutes. How many minutes does the sawing take?
exercise: dad's "between jobs" so he's cutting firewood. log's {len} dm, pieces {p} dm, {m} min a cut. how long, and don't you dare say {n*m}
test: Grandad's old ladder "gave up the ghost", so {a} saws its {len} cm rail into pieces {p} cm long. Each cut takes {m} seconds. How many seconds do all the cuts take?
exam: A log of length {len} decimetres is to be sawn into pieces each of length {p} decimetres. It is given that each individual cut requires {m} minutes. Determine the total time, in minutes, required for the sawing.
exam: Ascertain the duration, in seconds, of the cutting of a ribbon of {len} centimetres into pieces of {p} centimetres each, whereas each cut occupies {m} seconds.
exam: It is given that a pipe of {len} metres is divided by cutting into equal sections of {p} metres, each cut requiring {m} minutes of labour. State the aggregate duration of the labour, in minutes.
exam: Whereas {a} is engaged to divide a plank {len} decimetres in length into segments of {p} decimetres, and whereas each cut necessitates {m} minutes, compute the total number of minutes so expended.
